   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/3776-jp-phone` (head `ab40c7ea`, on upstream `6afbe3f3`) — a Japanese mobile in a CSV is masked.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/redact/redact.go` carries exactly one `PHONE` rule, `(?:\\+?86[- ]?)?1[3-9]\\d{9}` — China's mobile shape. `+81 90-1234-5678` matches nothing, and `modelFits`' `PHONE` case is shape-agnostic (7+ digits, not an epoch, not a decimal), so the local model never sees a span either.\n\n**Change.** one rule beside the Chinese one, `(?:\\+?81[- ]?|0)[789]0[- ]\\d{4}[- ]\\d{4}` with `bound: digits, cat: catPersonal`, and the eval's `GuardKnown: \"#3776\"` comes off — the case now comes out right, so the marker that excuses it would fail the eval.\n\n**Verified.** Red: `go test -tags nogui ./internal/redact/ -run TestMaskPhoneShapes` → `redact_test.go:106: \"90-1234-5678\" still in \"$ cat contacts.csv…\"` (3 of 7 cases)\nGreen: `same command → 8/8; `TestMaskEval` green, and the package's 95 tests pass` → `ok github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/redact`\n\nThe table also pins the shapes around it: bare `090-…`/`080-…`, `+86 138…` still masked, a Japanese landline (`+81 3-1234-5678`) and prose numbers (`v0.1.14`, `3.5s`) kept. The AstrLink Guard half needs nothing once the rule masks the number before a model is asked.\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 26's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6afbe3f3` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3776-jp-phone — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
